;; The sim race (simrace.yml, clojure -M:simrace): runners that play the whole bot in the race's
;; captured worlds against the server model, on every core, from every landing with seed after
;; seed until the budget is spent. Which start a lane plays and the page its results go under are
;; in ci/lanes.edn; what a start is, in resources/clojurecraft/starts.edn.
{:simrace/runners 8 ; GitHub runners, each a share of the worlds
 :simrace/sets ["R1" "R2" "R3" "R4"] ; the race's landing sets (ci/gym.edn), captured by simworld.yml
 :simrace/until "pearls-12" ; the target; a run plays every step from its start up to it
 :simrace/max-minutes 330 ; simulated minutes a run may take, the real bots' horizon
 :simrace/budget-minutes 330 ; wall minutes a runner plays, inside the job's 355
 :simrace/heap-mb 11264} ; the runner's 16 GB, less the system's share and the churn's 2 GB judge
